  "final_message": "I didn't do a straight rename. `OrderPlaced` now carries both the new and the old field names. All 39 tests pass.\n\nA straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume this event from other repos. ARCH-4 says changes must be additive and renames must go through deprecation.\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/core/events.ts`: `OrderPlaced` now has `createdAt` and `amountCents` with the same values as before. `placedAt` and `totalCents` stay as `@deprecated` aliases.\n- `schemaVersion` stays at 3, since the change is additive.\n- `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now assert the new fields alongside the old ones.\n- I left the `GET /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` responses alone. `GET /orders/{id}` is used by web-storefront (ARCH-8), and you only asked about the event.\n\n**Next steps for the actual rename**\n1. Have billing-service and analytics-ingest switch to `createdAt` and `amountCents`.\n2. Once they've deployed, remove `placedAt` and `totalCents` from the event. That removal is a breaking change, so it should be coordinated with those teams and probably go out as a schema version bump.\n\nIf you want the old fields removed now, I need confirmation that both consumers have already migrated.",
